{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringSelectionIndicator","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Configuring the Selection Indicator","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"BarKit"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Customize the animated highlight that tracks the selected item.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringLayout","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringBackground","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringItems","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringAnimations","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/TabBarIntegration","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/AdditionalConfiguration","doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringBadges"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The selection indicator is a rounded rectangle that moves between items when selection changes.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It is configured via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/SelectionIndicatorConfiguration"},{"text":", passed to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/BarConfiguration\/indicator"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" to disable the indicator entirely.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Color and border","anchor":"Color-and-border","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(","    indicator: .init(","        color: .white.opacity(0.2),","        border: .init(color: .white.opacity(0.4), lineWidth: 1)","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Insets","anchor":"Insets","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Control the gap between the indicator and the item frame:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(indicator: .init(inset: .init(top: 4, leading: 4, bottom: 4, trailing: 4)))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive values shrink the indicator, negative values expand it beyond the item bounds."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Transition animation","anchor":"Transition-animation","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The indicator moves between items with a configurable animation:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Spring (default)",".init(indicator: .init(transitionAnimation: .parameters(.init(type: .spring, duration: 0.4))))","","\/\/ Custom SwiftUI animation",".init(indicator: .init(transitionAnimation: .custom(.bouncy)))","","\/\/ Instant snap",".init(indicator: .init(transitionAnimation: nil))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Scale effect","anchor":"Scale-effect","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apply a brief scale pulse to the indicator during transition:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(indicator: .init(scaleEffect: .init(xScale: 1.3, yScale: 1.1, duration: 0.2)))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Drag gesture","anchor":"Drag-gesture","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default the user can drag the indicator between items. Disable if needed:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(indicator: .init(isDragGestureEnabled: false))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Metal shader effects","anchor":"Metal-shader-effects","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Visual effects applied at the indicator boundary, inspired by lens distortion and chromatic aberration."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Lens distortion","anchor":"Lens-distortion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Displaces pixels near the indicator edge, creating a subtle warping effect.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"zoneWidth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — width of the distortion zone in points (typical range 2.0–12.0)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"strength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — maximum pixel displacement (typical range 1.5–5.0)","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(indicator: .init(effects: [.lensDistortion(.init(zoneWidth: 12, strength: 2))]))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Chromatic aberration","anchor":"Chromatic-aberration","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Separates RGB channels near the indicator edge, creating a color fringe effect.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zoneWidth"},{"type":"text","text":" — width of the aberration zone in points (typical range 1.0–6.0)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"strength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — RGB channel separation in pixels (typical range 1.0–4.0)","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(indicator: .init(effects: [.chromaticAberration(.init(zoneWidth: 8, strength: 4))]))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both effects can be combined:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".init(indicator: .init(effects: [.lensDistortion(), .chromaticAberration()]))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both effects are inspired by their physical counterparts and do not attempt to model them accurately."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All Selection indicator configuration options are available interactively in the Example App under the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Selection indicator"}]},{"text":" settings section.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/barkit\/configuringselectionindicator"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://barkit.BarKit/documentation/BarKit/ConfiguringAnimations":{"title":"Configuring Animations","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/ConfiguringAnimations","url":"\/documentation\/barkit\/configuringanimations","kind":"article","abstract":[]},"doc://barkit.BarKit/documentation/BarKit/TabBarIntegration":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/TabBarIntegration","url":"\/documentation\/barkit\/tabbarintegration","role":"article","title":"Tab Bar Integration","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Use BarKit as a floating or pinned tab bar.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://barkit.BarKit/documentation/BarKit/AdditionalConfiguration":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/AdditionalConfiguration","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/barkit\/additionalconfiguration","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"article","title":"Additional Configuration"},"doc://barkit.BarKit/documentation/BarKit/GettingStarted":{"title":"Getting Started","url":"\/documentation\/barkit\/gettingstarted","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/barkit.BarKit\/documentation\/BarKit\/GettingStarted","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Add a customizable bar to your SwiftUI app in minutes.","type":"text"}]},"doc://barkit.BarKit/documentation/BarKit/ConfiguringBackground":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/barkit\/c